# Consecrated Sphinx and Notion Thief, both Bot1's. "Whenever an opponent draws a card" triggers on a card drawn (CR 603.2),
# and a draw Notion Thief replaces never happens (CR 614.6): Bot2 skips it. Bot2's turn 2 and turn 4 draws for the turn are
# exempt from Notion Thief (the first card of the draw step) and do trigger the Sphinx, whose two cards Bot1 takes each time
# - its own draws are no opponent's and Notion Thief leaves them alone. Bot2's Ancestral Recall on turn 4 is three draws that
# Notion Thief replaces: Bot1 draws those three, and the Sphinx does not trigger - nothing is on the stack once the spell has
# resolved.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Sol Ring
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Consecrated Sphinx
Notion Thief
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Ancestral Recall
Swamp x5
Swamp x20

